"overall": "This is a close, faithful rendering. It keeps the Septuagintal oddities (the cord, the friends honoured, 'no one in them', 'receive your cities in vain') and follows the tenses carefully. The one real fault is the plural 'ossos' in v. 15 for the singular 'os meum'. The rest are small matters of word order or added pronouns. The pointing marks (*, † in vv. 12 and 16, ‡ in v. 14) match the Latin in every verse."}
